e AC-5\"}},\"session_id\":\"bb1f3fcf-4d78-4a97-8c5b-320e502ce14a\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"9e4fcd7b-c1f1-41b8-8126-dc89e341ef32\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:2394:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_01Jmh6rUNpXVkX37CCJM9mJ4\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All gates pass and the diff is clean. The implementation is complete:\\n\\n- **Trigger gate** (`pipeline.ts`): the advance registration stays at its pinned first-before-poke site, throw-isolated; the callback now consults a flag set only when the walk records a `turn_end` (skipped duplicates never set it).\\n- **Decision reshape** (`boundary.ts`): zone rows carry `turn_id`, group consecutively (NULL → singleton), and the walk evicts whole oldest groups only while the post-eviction sum stays ≥ target; the open turn's group and the newest remaining group are never candidates.\\n- **Config** (`view.ts`/`profiles.ts`): two-field budgets, 64k/32k defaults, `max > target` validation, `floorTokens` rejected as unknown config.\\n- **Tests**: new `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` (TC-5.1/5.2/5.3, G2 worked golden, exact-target, newest-turn protection, turnless singleton); `view-boundary.test.ts` amended per the ledger; G1 trajectory golden re-cut for turn grouping; ripple amendments in `view-fixture`, `inspect-view`, `view-pull`; red-manifest regenerated; immutability check green.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\n  \\\"planSummary\\\": \\\"Gated the existing post-commit boundary-advance registration in intake's pipeline on a recorded turn_end (same registration site, ordering, and throw isolation); reshaped the boundary decision to whole-turn groups (turn_id-consecutive grouping, NULL as singleton) with the peek-ahead stop (evict only while remaining ≥ target) and protection f