{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md | sed -n '20,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t\n    21\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    22\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    23\t\n    24\t- **AC-5.1**: The advance check runs only when an intake batch commits a `turn_end`. Mid-turn batches never move the boundary regardless of zone size, and rendered bytes do not change between turn closes.\n    25\t- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\n    26\t- **AC-5.3**: The peek-ahead stop: a turn is evicted only if the zone's sum after evicting it remains ≥ target. The advance lands in [target, target + one turn). The newest closed turn is never evicted.\n    27\t- **AC-5.4**: Config is max and target with defaults 64k/32k; max > target validated with a caller error; the floor token budget is retired from the config surface.\n    28\t- **AC-5.5**: All other Epic 03 boundary contracts hold under the new trigger: forward-only, summary-else-truncation short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, post-commit seam with non-blocking failure visible in status.\n    29\t\n    30\t**Test Conditions**\n    31\t\n    32\t- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\n    33\t  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\n    34\t  - consecutive pulls during the open turn are byte-identical\n    35\t  - the batch closing the turn commits; exactly one advance runs\n    36\t  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\n    37\t  - no turn is partially flipped\n    38\t  - a small next turn closes under max and causes no movement\n    39\t  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\n    40\t- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3, AC-5.4): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\n    41\t  - golden G2: 30k/25k/20k/15k turns with 64k/32k budgets advances boundary after the 25k group and lands zone at 35k\n    42\t  - landing always falls in [target, target + one turn)\n    43\t  - exact-target variant advances through a turn when remaining sum is exactly target\n    44\t  - newest closed turn remains intact even when it alone exceeds target\n    45\t  - `maxTokens <= targetTokens` returns a caller `TypeError` naming the constraint\n    46\t  - defaults resolve to 64k/32k\n    47\t- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.5): amended `view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file\n    48\t  - flipped results stay flipped across later turn closes\n    49\t  - short form remains summary-when-ready else truncation\n    50\t  - compact resets boundary to the compact point with a fresh full tail\n    51\t  - same record plus same budgets replays to identical boundary trajectory\n    52\t  - injected `post-commit-advance` failure leaves intake unaffected, boundary unchanged, and status showing over-budget zone\n    53\t  - the next turn close heals the failed advance\n    54\t\n    55\t### Technical Design\n    56\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    57\t\n    58\t#### Architecture Context\n    59\t\n    60\tThis story patches Epic 03's visibility-boundary contract. The advance registration stays on the existing post-commit seam but is gated to batches that commit a `turn_end`; the decision function changes from message-grained eviction plus floor config to whole-turn groups plus peek-ahead target landing.\n    61\t\n    62\tThe storage shape does not migrate. `view_boundary` remains the stored boundary; `VisibilityBudgets` loses `floorTokens`, and the newest closed turn plus open-turn trigger rule replaces the old floor behavior.\n    63\t\n    64\t#### Build Strategy\n    65\t\n    66\tStrategy: full-staged-risk\n    67\t\n    68\tReason:\n    69\t- This changes a persisted read boundary, replay determinism, config validation, and an existing Epic 03 test surface.\n    70\t- The amendment ledger must be applied precisely so superseded tests are rewritten, not discarded.\n    71\t\n    72\tRisk Reminders:\n    73\t- Keep post-commit ordering and throw isolation unchanged.\n    74\t- Use whole-turn grouping by `turn_id`; turnless results become singleton groups.\n    75\t- Regenerate the red-manifest artifact after ledger amendments.\n    76\t\n    77\t#### Implementation Targets\n    78\t\n    79\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n    80\t|---|---|\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
